# PATCH: 004-restrict-downloads
#
# Blocks all file-save and download paths with four enforcement layers:
#
# 1. internalSave() (toolkit/content/contentAreaUtils.js)
#    Single JS funnel for all user-initiated saves: Ctrl+S, Save Page As,
#    Save Link As, Save Image As, and all context-menu save variants.
#    Returns immediately after showing a native alert.
#
# 2. nsExternalHelperAppService::CreateListener (uriloader/exthandler/)
#    Single C++ funnel for all HTTP-triggered downloads: Content-Disposition:
#    attachment, MIME-type sniffing, and <a download> anchor attribute.
#    Cancels the channel and returns NS_ERROR_ABORT after showing a native
#    alert. The channel cancel triggers the standard network error path,
#    which cleanly tears down the download without leaving partial files.
#
# 3. ShellService.canSetDesktopBackground (browser/components/shell/)
#    Returns false unconditionally, which suppresses the "Set as Desktop
#    Background" context menu item on macOS and Windows before it is shown.
#    This prevents images from being written to ~/Pictures/ via the shell
#    service, which uses nsIWebBrowserPersist and bypasses both funnels above.
#
# 4. nsMacShellService::SetDesktopBackground / nsWindowsShellService::SetDesktopBackground
#    Defense-in-depth block at the C++ shell service level in case the
#    function is reached by any path other than the context menu item.


diff --git a/browser/components/shell/ShellService.sys.mjs b/browser/components/shell/ShellService.sys.mjs
index 9d57af17c3f7..d10d696fbdbb 100644
